            "text": "{\n  \"resolutions\": [\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Creating, updating, rescheduling, canceling, or deleting events changes external state and requires confirmation. Confirm title, attendees, date, time, time zone, location, conferencing, and recurrence.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition applies. The user has provided the required confirmation details (event title, attendees, new date/time, time zone, location preference, conferencing, and recurrence). Proceed to reschedule the recurring 'Platform Sync' series now to Tuesday, 14 October 2026, 09:30\u201310:15 America/New_York, applying the change to the entire weekly series; keep the same four attendees (me, Lena Fischer, Marcus Bell, Aditi Shah); leave the physical location blank (no room); and preserve the existing Zoom link. Do the reschedule operation when calling the calendar tool.\"\n    ,\n      \"finding\": \"User request: \\\"Shift the weekly 'Platform Sync' event to Tuesday 14 October 2026, 09:30 to 10:15, America/New_York... Everything else stays put: the same four people on the invite (me, Lena Fischer, Marcus Bell, Aditi Shah), the same existing Zoom link, no physical room, and it stays the same weekly series with every future occurrence moving to that slot... Make the change on the calendar now, please.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Ask for confirmation before destructive actions. Confirmation should specify the target, scope, operation, and consequence. If ambiguity remains, ask a focused clarifying question.\",\n      \"directive\": \"Because the user explicitly instructed to make the change now and supplied the target, scope, and operation, treat that as the required confirmation and do not pause for additional general confirmation. If any ambiguity remains at runtime (for example, if the calendar tool shows multiple matching recurring events or multiple calendars), ask a focused clarifying question naming the ambiguous item (e.g., which specific recurring series or which calendar) before making a change.\"\n    ,\n      \"finding\": \"User: \\\"...I talked it through with all three of them on Friday and they are happy with the new time. Make the change on the calendar now, please.\\\" (user explicitly requests the change and states attendees agreed).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Use tools only when required or clearly helpful for the task. Do not call forbidden tools. Do not fabricate tool results. Do not expose raw tool JSON. If a tool fails, state the limitation and avoid pretending success.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition applies. After confirming that the requested details are the intended update (per above), call the available calendar tool to perform the reschedule. Do not fabricate results: capture the calendar tool's actual outcome and return a concise human-readable summary (not raw JSON). If the calendar tool reports an error or ambiguity (e.g., multiple matching recurring events, permission problems), report the exact problem and next steps.\"\n    ,\n      \"finding\": \"Declared context: tools available on this turn: calendar; operation: reschedule (user asked to \\\"Make the change on the calendar now, please.\\\").\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Calendar content is private. Minimize quoted private content. Do not infer sensitive attributes from calendar entries or metadata.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition applies. When communicating about the change, minimize private data exposure: only echo the attendees and details required to confirm the operation (as the user already provided). Do not include or expose any additional calendar metadata, email addresses, private URLs, authentication headers, or raw connector payloads in the response.\"\n    ,\n      \"",
